WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Do you want subtitles for any video?
-=[ ai.OpenSubtitles.com ]=-

2
00:00:47.672 --> 00:00:50.967
THE APARTMENT JOB

3
00:00:52.719 --> 00:00:54.387
I haven't introduced myself properly.

4
00:00:59.184 --> 00:01:00.894
I'm the president of Taesan Construction.

5
00:01:01.770 --> 00:01:02.896
Lee Chung-won.

6
00:01:17.327 --> 00:01:19.621
You seem to be great at finding things.

7
00:01:19.704 --> 00:01:21.873
so what are you looking for here
at Taesan Group?

8
00:01:22.916 --> 00:01:25.919
Whatever it is. I'm afraid
you won't be able to find it here.

9
00:01:26.878 --> 00:01:27.879
I feel sorry about that.

10
00:01:29.672 --> 00:01:31.883
No. I've already found it.

11
00:01:32.550 --> 00:01:35.595
You have control
over True Value's reserve fund.

12
00:01:35.678 --> 00:01:36.721
Come on.

13
00:01:37.597 --> 00:01:38.848
What do you mean?

14
00:01:40.391 --> 00:01:44.145
You got rid of President Seo.

15
00:01:44.229 --> 00:01:47.607
so you're making it difficult
for me to use my own money.

16
00:01:48.233 --> 00:01:49.943
I know I shouldn't.

17
00:01:50.527 --> 00:01:53.238
but I'm starting to resent you.

18
00:01:54.948 --> 00:01:57.158
<i>The moment I treat him like an enemy.</i>

19
00:01:57.242 --> 00:01:58.785
<i>the reserve fund goes out the window.</i>

20
00:01:59.452 --> 00:02:02.330
Then can't I just do

21
00:02:03.081 --> 00:02:05.834
what President Seo used to do?

22
00:02:08.795 --> 00:02:09.629
Why don't you

23
00:02:10.588 --> 00:02:13.800
let me become your right-hand man?

24
00:02:19.889 --> 00:02:21.432
My right-hand man?

25
00:02:22.016 --> 00:02:23.017
I'm quite competent.

26
00:02:23.101 --> 00:02:24.644
Of course.

27
00:02:24.727 --> 00:02:27.397
You became the president
by planting relics.

28
00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:29.691
Your planning. execution. and acting…

29
00:02:29.774 --> 00:02:31.693
I know how impressive you are.

30
00:02:31.776 --> 00:02:33.820
I'll be better than President Seo.

31
00:02:33.903 --> 00:02:36.948
President Seo was the keeper of my vault.

32
00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:40.368
Deposits. withdrawals.

33
00:02:40.451 --> 00:02:42.662
and moving money around.

34
00:02:42.745 --> 00:02:44.664
My keeper only has one job.

35
00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:47.000
To keep my money safe.

36
00:02:49.043 --> 00:02:50.086
That's

37
00:02:51.045 --> 00:02:51.963
it?

38
00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:56.426
But it's not an easy job.

39
00:02:56.509 --> 00:02:57.427
This place

40
00:02:57.510 --> 00:03:00.763
is filled with parasites
eating away at my fund.

41
00:03:00.847 --> 00:03:03.433
They're always asking for things.

42
00:03:04.601 --> 00:03:07.604
Why don't you give me a chance first.
then decide?

43
00:03:08.187 --> 00:03:09.230
How would I trust you?

44
00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:12.567
You came to empty out my vault.

45
00:03:13.776 --> 00:03:18.114
I only realized today
that the vault had an owner.

46
00:03:18.698 --> 00:03:19.782
And if there's an owner.

47
00:03:20.491 --> 00:03:21.910
I should suck up to them

48
00:03:23.161 --> 00:03:25.580
if I want to get any scraps.

49
00:03:27.081 --> 00:03:29.667
Okay. Then do as you like.

50
00:03:29.751 --> 00:03:33.713
I need to like you
to be able to trust you with my key.

51
00:03:34.422 --> 00:03:36.174
I don't work with just anyone.

52
00:03:48.603 --> 00:03:52.190
I can't believe the president here
was the penthouse jerk.

53
00:03:52.273 --> 00:03:54.192
You used to say you admired him.

54
00:03:54.692 --> 00:03:57.403
Taesan Construction really is huge.

55
00:03:59.405 --> 00:04:02.951
<i>Just wait and see how I take that key.</i>

56
00:04:08.581 --> 00:04:12.752
THE APARTMENT JOB

57
00:04:14.587 --> 00:04:16.381
{\an8}It's past dinnertime.

58
00:04:16.464 --> 00:04:18.841
{\an8}but no one's home yet.

59
00:04:18.925 --> 00:04:21.844
{\an8}Preparing meals wasn't in my contract.

60
00:04:21.928 --> 00:04:23.471
{\an8}Darn it.

61
00:04:23.554 --> 00:04:25.390
{\an8}I can't believe I'm doing this at my age.

62
00:04:26.224 --> 00:04:28.059
{\an8}Hey. come and eat!

63
00:04:29.060 --> 00:04:30.353
{\an8}Okay!

64
00:04:31.521 --> 00:04:35.358
{\an8}You're full of energy after your nap.

65
00:04:36.067 --> 00:04:38.236
{\an8}-Thank you.
-Enjoy.

66
00:04:47.328 --> 00:04:48.162
<i>His wife?</i>

67
00:04:48.746 --> 00:04:50.623
Why are you the president's wife?

68
00:04:50.707 --> 00:04:52.959
What the hell have you been up to?

69
00:04:53.543 --> 00:04:55.295
Ha-jeong. just calm down.

70
00:04:55.920 --> 00:04:57.964
Mr. Park is actually my client--

71
00:04:58.047 --> 00:04:58.923
Client?

72
00:05:00.550 --> 00:05:01.551
This won't do.

73
00:05:01.634 --> 00:05:04.053
I'm going to take this up
with your law firm.

74
00:05:04.137 --> 00:05:07.015
You didn't take the bar exam
to pretend to be someone's mom.

75
00:05:07.098 --> 00:05:09.058
Why would they waste
your talent like this?

76
00:05:09.142 --> 00:05:11.436
Come on. I'll go talk to them.

77
00:05:11.519 --> 00:05:13.062
No. Ha-jeong.

78
00:05:13.146 --> 00:05:14.689
Come on. Hurry up.

79
00:05:15.398 --> 00:05:16.232
Ha-jeong.

80
00:05:17.817 --> 00:05:18.735
Ha-jeong…

81
00:05:19.569 --> 00:05:21.195
I'm not a lawyer.

82
00:05:24.574 --> 00:05:26.576
What are you talking about?

83
00:05:27.285 --> 00:05:28.828
You're not a lawyer?

84
00:05:29.746 --> 00:05:30.872
Let's go.

85
00:05:32.874 --> 00:05:33.958
I'm not.

86
00:05:36.085 --> 00:05:37.211
Kang Ha-ri.

87
00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:39.797
What are you. if you're not a lawyer?

88
00:05:39.881 --> 00:05:41.674
What are you. then?

89
00:05:42.175 --> 00:05:44.469
Tell me! What are you?

90
00:05:46.804 --> 00:05:49.682
Mom… I mean. Ha-ri. Come and eat.

91
00:05:53.811 --> 00:05:55.229
Geez.

92
00:05:55.313 --> 00:05:57.940
Your father-in-law
prepared dinner for you.

93
00:05:58.024 --> 00:06:00.276
At least pretend to have a bite.

94
00:06:00.359 --> 00:06:02.862
I don't have an appetite. Eat without me.

95
00:06:03.529 --> 00:06:06.365
Then just come
and have some eggs at least…

96
00:06:07.742 --> 00:06:10.161
Hey. you shouldn't have eaten
all that by yourself.

97
00:06:11.120 --> 00:06:14.624
Protein is important for growing children.

98
00:06:16.084 --> 00:06:17.585
Fine. Eat.

99
00:06:19.170 --> 00:06:21.005
You're not eating any soup. are you?

100
00:06:22.048 --> 00:06:23.674
The smell.

101
00:06:26.010 --> 00:06:27.428
I'm going home.

102
00:06:30.264 --> 00:06:31.849
Get home safely.

103
00:06:32.642 --> 00:06:35.019
Lizard. did something happen to her?

104
00:06:35.728 --> 00:06:38.981
I don't know. She's been like that
ever since picking up the kid.

105
00:06:39.482 --> 00:06:41.609
See that sunken spot on the sofa?

106
00:06:41.692 --> 00:06:43.861
She sat there all day.

107
00:06:43.945 --> 00:06:46.072
blankly staring out the window.

108
00:06:46.155 --> 00:06:48.282
Gyeong-buk.
is something going on with her?

109
00:06:50.493 --> 00:06:53.496
She just needs time to herself sometimes.

110
00:06:53.996 --> 00:06:56.082
Don't you even know that?

111
00:06:58.626 --> 00:07:01.379
If he knew.
he wouldn't be all alone. would he?

112
00:07:01.462 --> 00:07:02.588
Gyeong-buk's all grown up.

113
00:07:04.340 --> 00:07:06.342
Where are you. Yeong-ju?

114
00:07:06.425 --> 00:07:08.427
I opened a can since I was so frustrated.

115
00:07:08.928 --> 00:07:10.847
You'd better come before I'm done.

116
00:07:20.606 --> 00:07:22.191
<i>A stand-in service?</i>

117
00:07:23.734 --> 00:07:25.862
You're joking. right?

118
00:07:25.945 --> 00:07:27.155
That can't be true.

119
00:07:28.865 --> 00:07:31.784
I was given a job to play the role
of Park Hae-kang's wife.

120
00:07:35.288 --> 00:07:36.205
How…

121
00:07:38.916 --> 00:07:40.668
-How…
-Ha-jeong.

122
00:07:42.628 --> 00:07:45.548
How could you deceive me like this?

123
00:07:46.716 --> 00:07:49.385
I worked so hard
to help you become a lawyer.

124
00:07:49.469 --> 00:07:51.846
How could you do this to me?

125
00:07:52.805 --> 00:07:54.098
I never asked you to!

126
00:07:55.641 --> 00:07:58.853
Just stop.
I'm sick of hearing you say that!

127
00:08:00.563 --> 00:08:01.981
Don't do anything anymore.

128
00:08:02.064 --> 00:08:03.816
I know it's hard for you.

129
00:08:03.900 --> 00:08:06.319
so just don't do anything for me anymore!

130
00:08:13.743 --> 00:08:14.660
You're the worst.

131
00:08:19.332 --> 00:08:20.791
You're so shameless.

132
00:08:21.459 --> 00:08:22.376
You're…

133
00:08:24.045 --> 00:08:25.755
seriously messed up.

134
00:08:29.717 --> 00:08:30.843
Ms. Kang.

135
00:08:36.307 --> 00:08:37.725
Were you crying?

136
00:08:50.488 --> 00:08:51.697
Mr. Park.

137
00:08:54.450 --> 00:08:57.662
My sister practically raised me.

138
00:08:59.080 --> 00:09:01.040
I thought that was only natural.

139
00:09:01.874 --> 00:09:04.001
but it feels like a luxury to me now.

140
00:09:06.003 --> 00:09:08.214
I have a debt like that too.

141
00:09:10.675 --> 00:09:12.510
There's someone

142
00:09:12.593 --> 00:09:15.555
who took me in and protected me
instead of my father.

143
00:09:18.140 --> 00:09:19.183
He…

144
00:09:20.268 --> 00:09:22.103
doesn't want anything in return.

145
00:09:23.521 --> 00:09:25.439
but I still want to repay him.

146
00:09:27.275 --> 00:09:28.985
It's not because I feel indebted.

147
00:09:30.194 --> 00:09:31.362
but because I'm grateful.

148
00:09:33.990 --> 00:09:35.491
It was heartwarming.

149
00:09:37.994 --> 00:09:38.828
However.

150
00:09:40.037 --> 00:09:41.539
do you know that such debts

151
00:09:42.373 --> 00:09:45.793
sometimes give us the motivation to go on?

152
00:09:48.045 --> 00:09:48.921
You're right.

153
00:09:51.007 --> 00:09:53.801
But now.

154
00:09:53.884 --> 00:09:57.096
I'm not even sure if my dream
is actually mine

155
00:09:57.179 --> 00:09:58.973
or my sister's.

156
00:09:59.724 --> 00:10:02.935
My failure feels like
my sister's failure now.

157
00:10:04.020 --> 00:10:05.896
Isn't it okay to fail?

158
00:10:07.398 --> 00:10:09.066
Why should I fail?

159
00:10:09.692 --> 00:10:12.320
Some things grow clearer when you fail.

160
00:10:13.362 --> 00:10:16.657
You sometimes see things
that you weren't able to see before.

161
00:10:17.658 --> 00:10:20.745
Then what did you see after failing?

162
00:10:26.459 --> 00:10:27.376
People.

163
00:10:28.210 --> 00:10:29.962
The people who are protecting me.

164
00:10:30.630 --> 00:10:32.340
and the people I should protect.

165
00:10:37.720 --> 00:10:42.433
So you should take a look
at what you see after failing too.

166
00:10:47.480 --> 00:10:50.316
Why are you suddenly sounding so cool?

167
00:10:52.401 --> 00:10:53.819
YEONG-JU

168
00:10:53.903 --> 00:10:55.571
Oh. right. Yeong-ju!

169
00:10:56.530 --> 00:10:58.074
What do I do?

170
00:11:00.660 --> 00:11:02.953
{\an8}SEOUL JUNGBU DETENTION CENTER

171
00:11:03.037 --> 00:11:06.540
{\an8}<i>Inmate No. 3417. Park Yong-man.</i>
<i>is in the infirmary.</i>

172
00:11:06.624 --> 00:11:08.668
{\an8}<i>No visitors are allowed</i>
<i>due to health reasons.</i>

173
00:11:20.346 --> 00:11:21.889
MR. SON. SEOUL POLICE CHIEF

174
00:11:30.523 --> 00:11:32.441
You asshole. Have you lost your mind?

175
00:11:32.525 --> 00:11:34.527
How dare you come here?

176
00:11:34.610 --> 00:11:37.488
Release Yong-man on medical bail first.

177
00:11:37.571 --> 00:11:40.241
-The money will be ready soon.
-It doesn't work that way.

178
00:11:40.324 --> 00:11:41.575
Bring the money first!

179
00:11:41.659 --> 00:11:43.702
He's sick!

180
00:11:43.786 --> 00:11:45.204
The elderly are always sick.

181
00:11:48.207 --> 00:11:49.625
If anything happens to him.

182
00:11:50.835 --> 00:11:52.086
you won't get your ten billion.

183
00:11:52.169 --> 00:11:54.380
Are you out of your mind?

184
00:11:55.548 --> 00:11:57.425
How dare you threaten me like that?

185
00:11:57.508 --> 00:11:59.051
Are you acting like a thug again?

186
00:11:59.135 --> 00:12:00.469
Damn it.

187
00:12:01.720 --> 00:12:02.972
You little brat.

188
00:12:13.315 --> 00:12:14.275
Mr. Park.

189
00:12:15.401 --> 00:12:16.569
Park Hae-kang.

190
00:12:17.236 --> 00:12:18.404
Get a grip.

191
00:12:24.160 --> 00:12:25.202
I can't get him released.

192
00:12:26.454 --> 00:12:28.664
But I'll let him get treatment outside.

193
00:12:28.747 --> 00:12:29.665
Anything else

194
00:12:29.748 --> 00:12:31.792
will be discussed
after you bring the money.

195
00:13:03.532 --> 00:13:06.577
The invisible hand is the president
of the construction company?

196
00:13:07.912 --> 00:13:09.246
He's something else.

197
00:13:09.330 --> 00:13:11.790
He's taking money
from the apartment complex that he built?

198
00:13:12.625 --> 00:13:13.709
How creative.

199
00:13:13.792 --> 00:13:16.462
But shouldn't we report this?

200
00:13:17.046 --> 00:13:19.381
Why don't you report all of us then?

201
00:13:20.341 --> 00:13:22.384
Oh. we were going to do
the same thing. Sorry.

202
00:13:22.468 --> 00:13:24.929
Boss. what are you planning to do now?

203
00:13:26.055 --> 00:13:27.097
First.

204
00:13:27.890 --> 00:13:30.518
I'm going to become
Lee Chung-won's vault keeper.

205
00:13:30.601 --> 00:13:32.478
-What?
-His keeper?

206
00:13:32.561 --> 00:13:33.395
Right.

207
00:13:33.479 --> 00:13:38.025
You need the vault's key
to steal that fund.

208
00:13:38.108 --> 00:13:41.946
But would Lee Chung-won
give you that position?

209
00:13:42.655 --> 00:13:44.490
I'll make sure he has no other choice.

210
00:13:45.699 --> 00:13:47.493
Let's go meet President Seo first.

211
00:13:47.993 --> 00:13:49.411
Go and look for him.

212
00:13:49.495 --> 00:13:50.913
-Yes. sir.
-Yes. sir.

213
00:14:07.221 --> 00:14:08.722
MAIL ARRIVAL NOTICE

214
00:14:15.938 --> 00:14:16.814
What is it?

215
00:14:17.731 --> 00:14:18.899
His card statement.

216
00:14:20.776 --> 00:14:23.070
But there aren't any recent transactions.

217
00:14:23.737 --> 00:14:25.781
He uses his card for everything.

218
00:14:27.116 --> 00:14:30.119
I can tell what's going on.

219
00:14:30.828 --> 00:14:31.787
What do you mean?

220
00:14:32.580 --> 00:14:33.539
It's just like me.

221
00:14:33.622 --> 00:14:35.249
I can't use my card either.

222
00:14:35.833 --> 00:14:38.669
Can't you track his location or anything?

223
00:14:38.752 --> 00:14:40.880
I can't. His phone is turned off.

224
00:14:40.963 --> 00:14:43.966
What? He really is doing
the exact same thing I'm doing.

225
00:14:44.550 --> 00:14:46.176
I can't turn on my phone either.

226
00:14:46.260 --> 00:14:47.887
I just leave it somewhere warm

227
00:14:47.970 --> 00:14:50.848
and use it to iron my clothes.

228
00:14:50.931 --> 00:14:52.725
Good for you.

229
00:14:53.392 --> 00:14:54.560
Wait.

230
00:14:54.643 --> 00:14:56.770
President Seo went on a trip abroad?

231
00:14:56.854 --> 00:14:58.355
I don't know.

232
00:14:58.439 --> 00:15:00.441
He just sent a text
saying he's going overseas.

233
00:15:00.524 --> 00:15:02.276
He betrayed us.

234
00:15:02.359 --> 00:15:05.571
Traveling abroad
after the mess he created?

235
00:15:05.654 --> 00:15:06.989
Just forget him.

236
00:15:08.240 --> 00:15:11.577
We've decided to side
with the new president now.

237
00:15:11.660 --> 00:15:15.414
so please put in a good word for us
with President Park.

238
00:15:17.207 --> 00:15:18.834
You can rely on me.

239
00:15:18.918 --> 00:15:21.462
I'm Hae-kang's right-hand man.

240
00:15:21.545 --> 00:15:23.297
Is that so?

241
00:15:23.380 --> 00:15:25.883
Would you like to have anything else?

242
00:15:29.595 --> 00:15:30.679
Then can I order

243
00:15:30.763 --> 00:15:33.098
another large tea?

244
00:15:34.224 --> 00:15:36.602
You might feel sick
from a blood sugar spike.

245
00:15:36.685 --> 00:15:38.103
Drink some water. Water. please.

246
00:15:38.187 --> 00:15:39.647
Get us a big cup of water.

247
00:15:39.730 --> 00:15:41.899
Please give us another big cup of tea.

248
00:15:42.733 --> 00:15:43.943
-This too.
-Rice cakes.

249
00:15:44.026 --> 00:15:45.778
More rice cakes too!

250
00:15:48.739 --> 00:15:50.699
-President Seo?
-Yes.

251
00:15:51.367 --> 00:15:54.328
What kind of work did he normally do here?

252
00:15:55.287 --> 00:15:57.247
I'd like to learn what he did

253
00:15:57.331 --> 00:15:59.249
and think about what to do
as the president--

254
00:15:59.333 --> 00:16:00.584
Geez.

255
00:16:02.252 --> 00:16:04.755
Just thinking about that asshole

256
00:16:04.838 --> 00:16:07.967
makes my blood pressure rise
and gives me a headache.

257
00:16:08.050 --> 00:16:11.679
He was acting as though
he were True Value's king…

258
00:16:11.762 --> 00:16:12.680
King?

259
00:16:15.057 --> 00:16:18.644
If I wrote down
every terrible thing he did.

260
00:16:18.727 --> 00:16:21.605
there would be enough
for a full-length novel.

261
00:16:21.689 --> 00:16:25.484
I'm not even sure where I should start.

262
00:16:25.567 --> 00:16:27.528
Right. The most ridiculous one.

263
00:16:27.611 --> 00:16:31.031
He bought water with the maintenance fees.

264
00:16:32.908 --> 00:16:36.412
He ordered water every month
with the fees.

265
00:16:36.495 --> 00:16:39.873
<i>and when they were delivered</i>
<i>to the office.</i>

266
00:16:39.957 --> 00:16:43.794
<i>the security guards</i>
<i>brought them to his house.</i>

267
00:16:44.336 --> 00:16:45.879
To his house?

268
00:16:45.963 --> 00:16:47.297
Seriously.

269
00:16:47.381 --> 00:16:50.217
it's not like water costs a fortune.

270
00:16:50.300 --> 00:16:51.677
How cheap is that?

271
00:16:51.760 --> 00:16:54.304
And does he think the guards
are his errand boys?

272
00:16:54.388 --> 00:16:55.472
He orders them around.

273
00:16:55.556 --> 00:16:59.101
His abuse of power is on another level.

274
00:17:00.811 --> 00:17:02.980
And you know what's really funny?

275
00:17:03.772 --> 00:17:07.526
Did you know that the cleaning staff

276
00:17:07.609 --> 00:17:10.863
have been growing gardens on the rooftops?

277
00:17:10.946 --> 00:17:13.949
No. There are gardens on the rooftops?

278
00:17:14.533 --> 00:17:18.620
At first. I thought
they were just doing that as a hobby.

279
00:17:18.704 --> 00:17:21.081
so I was going to turn a blind eye.

280
00:17:21.165 --> 00:17:22.041
-But…
-Yes?

281
00:17:22.124 --> 00:17:24.126
It turns out that they were delivering

282
00:17:24.209 --> 00:17:26.545
all the vegetables from their gardens

283
00:17:26.628 --> 00:17:29.423
to President Seo's house.

284
00:17:30.716 --> 00:17:32.551
He didn't even let them use pesticides

285
00:17:32.634 --> 00:17:34.762
because he wanted
to eat organic vegetables.

286
00:17:34.845 --> 00:17:37.765
<i>And the cleaning staff were too scared</i>
<i>of getting fired to protest.</i>

287
00:17:37.848 --> 00:17:40.934
<i>They were farming</i>
<i>on top of all the cleaning work.</i>

288
00:17:41.018 --> 00:17:43.062
How can we call him human?

289
00:17:43.145 --> 00:17:46.648
But you didn't say anything
when he was doing all that?

290
00:17:46.732 --> 00:17:48.984
Why wouldn't I?
I'm Jang Suk-jin. you know.

291
00:17:49.068 --> 00:17:50.277
Of course. I said something.

292
00:17:50.360 --> 00:17:52.696
But that bastard didn't even blink an eye.

293
00:17:53.947 --> 00:17:56.283
I could talk about this endlessly.

294
00:17:56.366 --> 00:17:59.078
But do you know the worst thing

295
00:17:59.161 --> 00:18:00.245
about President Seo?

296
00:18:01.080 --> 00:18:04.541
He opposes every single thing

297
00:18:04.625 --> 00:18:06.960
that the residents request or suggest.

298
00:18:07.044 --> 00:18:08.170
{\an8}2021. RESIDENTS' ASSOCIATION MEETING

299
00:18:08.253 --> 00:18:10.422
{\an8}Why do they keep refusing
to do the repairs?

300
00:18:11.090 --> 00:18:14.927
It seems like the construction company
thinks we're pushovers.

301
00:18:15.010 --> 00:18:17.763
We have to do something about this.
don't you think?

302
00:18:17.846 --> 00:18:19.556
-Right.
-He's right.

303
00:18:19.640 --> 00:18:22.726
I understand what you mean.

304
00:18:22.810 --> 00:18:24.770
but we're up against a large company.

305
00:18:24.853 --> 00:18:28.607
Can you guarantee
that we'll win a lawsuit against them?

306
00:18:28.690 --> 00:18:31.777
And if word spreads
about our apartments having defects.

307
00:18:31.860 --> 00:18:33.487
property values will drop.

308
00:18:33.570 --> 00:18:35.030
Will you be okay with that?

309
00:18:36.365 --> 00:18:38.742
A new seafood stew place opened nearby.

310
00:18:38.826 --> 00:18:42.538
I'll give you a detailed explanation
over dinner there later.

311
00:18:42.621 --> 00:18:43.914
So please. sit down.

312
00:18:52.089 --> 00:18:54.049
In any case.

313
00:18:54.133 --> 00:18:57.803
President Seo was a pro
at stopping anyone from filing a lawsuit.

314
00:18:58.762 --> 00:19:00.764
And he harassed all the building reps

315
00:19:00.848 --> 00:19:02.307
who had any complaints

316
00:19:02.391 --> 00:19:06.228
and made them all give up
and move away in the end.

317
00:19:06.311 --> 00:19:11.358
Then he placed his own people
in those empty seats.

318
00:19:11.441 --> 00:19:14.444
He's a filthy fraud.

319
00:19:14.528 --> 00:19:17.906
Just thinking about him
makes my blood boil.

320
00:19:19.783 --> 00:19:21.201
<i>He stopped the lawsuits</i>

321
00:19:21.285 --> 00:19:24.663
<i>against Lee Chung-won's companies</i>
<i>and protected his money.</i>

322
00:19:24.746 --> 00:19:27.958
My keeper only has one job.

323
00:19:28.834 --> 00:19:30.127
To keep my money safe.

324
00:19:31.044 --> 00:19:32.880
<i>I get what I have to do.</i>

325
00:19:32.963 --> 00:19:35.382
<i>but will that be enough</i>
<i>to become one of his men?</i>

326
00:19:38.260 --> 00:19:40.971
<i>I need something with real impact.</i>

327
00:19:42.181 --> 00:19:44.141
<i>Something big.</i>

328
00:19:47.686 --> 00:19:48.896
Hello. ma'am.

329
00:19:50.772 --> 00:19:52.024
Hello.

330
00:19:53.358 --> 00:19:54.735
Were you buying groceries?

331
00:19:56.778 --> 00:19:57.779
Yes.

332
00:19:57.863 --> 00:20:00.741
We have business in Complex 2.
so excuse us.

333
00:20:00.824 --> 00:20:03.160
Bye. Take care. ma'am.

334
00:20:07.039 --> 00:20:08.665
She's so cold.

335
00:20:10.125 --> 00:20:11.752
Well. I'm the one at fault.

336
00:20:13.128 --> 00:20:15.172
Do I have to sleep
at Yeong-ju's again tonight?

337
00:20:22.846 --> 00:20:23.931
Wait!

338
00:20:26.433 --> 00:20:27.559
Were you out?

339
00:20:27.643 --> 00:20:28.936
I went to the supermarket.

340
00:20:29.436 --> 00:20:30.729
I got some boneless mackerel.

341
00:20:30.812 --> 00:20:34.566
Mr. Hwang said it's hard to debone fish
because of his eyesight.

342
00:20:35.234 --> 00:20:36.360
Who's Mr. Hwang?

343
00:20:37.527 --> 00:20:40.948
The man you call the Lizard
and treat harshly.

344
00:20:43.283 --> 00:20:46.161
You should've told Big Guy
to run errands like that.

345
00:20:46.662 --> 00:20:49.706
He said something about boneless fish
not being real fish.

346
00:20:49.790 --> 00:20:51.708
so he can't feed it to the kid.

347
00:20:51.792 --> 00:20:53.835
He has some weird philosophy about it.

348
00:20:53.919 --> 00:20:57.047
Big Guy has some serious opinions
when it comes to food.

349
00:20:57.547 --> 00:20:59.925
Life isn't that complicated though.

350
00:21:00.008 --> 00:21:02.052
We're just paying for convenience.

351
00:21:02.135 --> 00:21:03.136
What's the big deal?

352
00:21:09.476 --> 00:21:10.352
Are you okay?

353
00:21:22.906 --> 00:21:24.074
Excuse me.

354
00:21:24.157 --> 00:21:26.618
The elevator in Building 114 is broken.

355
00:21:26.702 --> 00:21:29.246
The president's in here.
Please take care of this quickly.

356
00:21:29.329 --> 00:21:30.789
<i>Just a moment. ma'am.</i>

357
00:21:34.835 --> 00:21:35.794
That startled me.

358
00:21:36.461 --> 00:21:39.464
I heard the elevators
are always breaking down.

359
00:21:39.965 --> 00:21:42.509
You're the president.
Can't you take care of this?

360
00:21:42.592 --> 00:21:43.885
You could just replace them all.

361
00:21:43.969 --> 00:21:46.638
The long-term repair reserve fund
shouldn't be used so rashly.

362
00:21:47.347 --> 00:21:48.557
Rashly?

363
00:21:48.640 --> 00:21:50.767
You're resolving
an inconvenience with money.

364
00:21:51.351 --> 00:21:53.854
Imagine having to use the stairs
every day instead.

365
00:21:53.937 --> 00:21:56.523
Everyone will be demanding
that the fund be used.

366
00:21:57.357 --> 00:21:59.818
Koreans can't stand any inconvenience.

367
00:21:59.901 --> 00:22:02.696
They'll gladly pay
to make life more convenient.

368
00:22:03.363 --> 00:22:06.783
They buy convenience.
like this boneless mackerel.

369
00:22:12.080 --> 00:22:13.248
It's working now.

370
00:22:14.875 --> 00:22:15.709
Let's go.

371
00:22:21.965 --> 00:22:23.258
RESIDENTS' ASSOCIATION MEETING

372
00:22:23.342 --> 00:22:24.718
Thank you for your suggestions.

373
00:22:24.801 --> 00:22:25.802
To summarize.

374
00:22:25.886 --> 00:22:28.347
replacing the equipment
in the community center gym.

375
00:22:28.430 --> 00:22:31.391
toys for the kids cafe.
a donation to the senior center.

376
00:22:31.475 --> 00:22:33.727
and repainting the exterior walls.

377
00:22:33.810 --> 00:22:36.146
Yes. those are the main suggestions.

378
00:22:36.229 --> 00:22:37.397
All right.

379
00:22:37.481 --> 00:22:39.274
The suggestions you've made

380
00:22:39.357 --> 00:22:40.984
are about making a better environment

381
00:22:41.068 --> 00:22:43.195
and improving resident services here.

382
00:22:43.278 --> 00:22:46.782
I also believe
all of these things are necessary.

383
00:22:46.865 --> 00:22:49.534
But to resolve all these problems.

384
00:22:49.618 --> 00:22:51.203
you know we need money. don't you?

385
00:22:53.121 --> 00:22:54.498
It all requires money.

386
00:22:54.581 --> 00:22:55.540
Money's the problem.

387
00:22:56.208 --> 00:22:59.169
That is why I'm suggesting
a 100% increase in the reserve fund

388
00:22:59.878 --> 00:23:03.006
for the present and future
of our apartment complex.

389
00:23:03.090 --> 00:23:04.758
What? 100%?

390
00:23:04.841 --> 00:23:05.967
100%?

391
00:23:07.302 --> 00:23:08.804
Isn't 100% too much?

392
00:23:11.973 --> 00:23:14.601
What? A 100% increase?

393
00:23:14.684 --> 00:23:16.353
What's gotten into him?

394
00:23:16.436 --> 00:23:18.939
What the heck is he thinking?

395
00:23:19.022 --> 00:23:21.149
That took quite a surprising turn.

396
00:23:21.233 --> 00:23:23.860
It does make me look forward
to the next episode.

397
00:23:26.696 --> 00:23:27.572
Yes. go on.

398
00:23:28.323 --> 00:23:30.283
Can't we cover
all the proposals from today

399
00:23:30.367 --> 00:23:33.370
with the reserve fund
that we already have right now?

400
00:23:33.453 --> 00:23:35.997
This apartment complex
is nearly ten years old now.

401
00:23:36.081 --> 00:23:37.666
More and more repairs will be needed.

402
00:23:37.749 --> 00:23:40.377
If we keep using
the reserve fund every time.

403
00:23:40.460 --> 00:23:42.170
we won't have anything left.

404
00:23:42.796 --> 00:23:45.257
To invest in improving
our living environment

405
00:23:45.340 --> 00:23:47.968
and carry out future repair plans.

406
00:23:48.051 --> 00:23:51.179
an increase in the reserve fund fee
is inevitable.

407
00:23:52.889 --> 00:23:53.807
Excuse me.

408
00:23:53.890 --> 00:23:56.768
I get all that.

409
00:23:56.852 --> 00:23:58.979
but if you're going to increase the fee.

410
00:23:59.062 --> 00:24:01.648
-you should do it gradually.
-Exactly.

411
00:24:01.731 --> 00:24:04.985
You can't just increase it
by 100% so suddenly.

412
00:24:05.068 --> 00:24:07.195
-That's a bit too much.
-Yeah.

413
00:24:08.321 --> 00:24:09.573
Our apartment complex

414
00:24:09.656 --> 00:24:12.367
has never raised the fee
since it was occupied.

415
00:24:12.450 --> 00:24:15.704
If you factor in inflation.
the amount hasn't changed on paper.

416
00:24:15.787 --> 00:24:18.748
but its real value
has been decreasing every year.

417
00:24:19.332 --> 00:24:20.458
To put it simply.

418
00:24:20.542 --> 00:24:24.087
you've been getting a discount
on the fee every year.

419
00:24:24.171 --> 00:24:28.049
Well. you're not wrong.

420
00:24:28.133 --> 00:24:29.050
but still…

421
00:24:29.134 --> 00:24:31.261
We live in a large apartment complex.

422
00:24:31.344 --> 00:24:34.514
Even a small repair
would be a huge project.

423
00:24:35.098 --> 00:24:36.641
With the reserve fund we have now.

424
00:24:36.725 --> 00:24:39.186
we won't be fully prepared
for future maintenance.

425
00:24:40.270 --> 00:24:42.355
But nothing is that urgent right now.

426
00:24:42.439 --> 00:24:44.608
A 100% increase is too much.

427
00:24:44.691 --> 00:24:45.650
That's what I'm saying.

428
00:24:46.776 --> 00:24:49.696
But President Park does have a point.

429
00:24:50.530 --> 00:24:52.407
There are apartment complexes
similar to ours.

430
00:24:52.490 --> 00:24:54.951
but they have much higher fees.

431
00:24:56.119 --> 00:24:58.496
-Yeah.
-Right.

432
00:25:01.333 --> 00:25:02.751
I agree as well.

433
00:25:02.834 --> 00:25:06.171
More and more problems
will come up as time passes.

434
00:25:06.838 --> 00:25:09.466
so it won't be a bad idea
to prepare in advance.

435
00:25:09.549 --> 00:25:10.717
-Right?
-Yes.

436
00:25:12.636 --> 00:25:13.929
You're right.

437
00:25:14.012 --> 00:25:17.641
If it's never been increased before.
I guess it's about time.

438
00:25:17.724 --> 00:25:20.852
Prices have gone up a lot over the years.

439
00:25:20.936 --> 00:25:24.272
Still. I believe
a 100% increase is too much.

440
00:25:24.356 --> 00:25:26.524
Right. I understand
your reason for opposing.

441
00:25:26.608 --> 00:25:28.860
That's why I'd like to hold

442
00:25:29.527 --> 00:25:31.821
a residents' vote this weekend.

443
00:25:32.322 --> 00:25:35.075
A residents' vote. That's a good idea.

444
00:25:36.284 --> 00:25:38.203
He's forward-thinking.

445
00:25:42.082 --> 00:25:45.085
But do you really agree
to raising the reserve fund fee?

446
00:25:45.168 --> 00:25:46.378
Of course not!

447
00:25:47.420 --> 00:25:48.797
Then why?

448
00:25:49.297 --> 00:25:51.341
We need to get on his good side.

449
00:25:51.424 --> 00:25:53.969
We have to show him
that we're all on his side

450
00:25:54.052 --> 00:25:56.137
to win some brownie points.

451
00:25:57.222 --> 00:25:59.766
But what if he really increases the fee?

452
00:25:59.849 --> 00:26:01.518
It's a 100% increase.

453
00:26:01.601 --> 00:26:04.604
He can't. We're doing a vote.

454
00:26:04.688 --> 00:26:06.898
The residents aren't crazy.

455
00:26:06.982 --> 00:26:08.942
Why would they agree to that?

456
00:26:09.025 --> 00:26:12.153
Then we just have to pretend
to support his proposal.

457
00:26:12.237 --> 00:26:14.572
-then vote against it.
-That's right.

458
00:26:17.659 --> 00:26:20.578
A proposal to raise
the reserve fund fee by 100%?

459
00:26:22.455 --> 00:26:24.457
Is this the plan you prepared?

460
00:26:24.541 --> 00:26:25.917
A meaningless vote?

461
00:26:26.001 --> 00:26:28.586
Boss. this really doesn't make any sense.

462
00:26:28.670 --> 00:26:29.754
It's impossible.

463
00:26:29.838 --> 00:26:32.173
It's the cost of a whole chicken
plus cheese balls.

464
00:26:32.674 --> 00:26:34.217
It's way too much.

465
00:26:34.301 --> 00:26:35.468
Just wait.

466
00:26:36.970 --> 00:26:38.638
More than half the residents

467
00:26:39.556 --> 00:26:41.308
will vote yes in the end.

468
00:26:47.897 --> 00:26:49.357
When are you coming home?

469
00:26:50.108 --> 00:26:51.776
I'll come when I come.

470
00:26:51.860 --> 00:26:52.986
You brat.

471
00:26:54.237 --> 00:26:55.655
I told you not to wear this.

472
00:26:56.239 --> 00:26:58.616
-You're wearing it again?
-Mom. there are people here.

473
00:27:00.869 --> 00:27:01.870
What's going on?

474
00:27:01.953 --> 00:27:03.788
What? Did it just stop?

475
00:27:03.872 --> 00:27:06.291
Is this working? Hello?

476
00:27:07.334 --> 00:27:08.626
Mr. Choi!

477
00:27:09.419 --> 00:27:11.129
The elevator stopped!

478
00:27:12.630 --> 00:27:14.507
{\an8}ELEVATOR UNDER MAINTENANCE

479
00:27:20.305 --> 00:27:22.682
Why is it so hard
just to smoke a cigarette?

480
00:27:25.894 --> 00:27:28.480
Mom. my legs hurt. Carry me.

481
00:27:28.563 --> 00:27:30.065
My legs hurt too.

482
00:27:30.148 --> 00:27:31.358
Carry me!

483
00:27:32.484 --> 00:27:33.443
We're late. Come on.

484
00:27:33.526 --> 00:27:36.029
-I'll be late for kindergarten!
-All right.

485
00:27:36.112 --> 00:27:37.697
There it is. Oh. hello.

486
00:27:38.573 --> 00:27:39.699
I can't believe this!

487
00:27:41.076 --> 00:27:43.119
-Why's it like this every day?
-You're so fast.

488
00:27:44.120 --> 00:27:46.122
Yes. Building 107? We're so sorry.

489
00:27:46.206 --> 00:27:47.582
We're checking right now.

490
00:27:47.665 --> 00:27:49.584
Yes. the repair company is on its way.

491
00:27:49.667 --> 00:27:50.919
Building 212 too?

492
00:27:51.002 --> 00:27:52.504
If you can wait just a moment…

493
00:27:52.587 --> 00:27:55.757
It's the first time
so many have broken down at once.

494
00:27:56.299 --> 00:27:58.718
Is the repair company still not answering?

495
00:28:00.011 --> 00:28:01.137
-Call them again.
-Okay.

496
00:28:03.098 --> 00:28:05.016
We'll do our best
to take care of this issue

497
00:28:05.100 --> 00:28:06.226
as soon as possible.

498
00:28:06.309 --> 00:28:08.311
-Come on.
-When?

499
00:28:10.313 --> 00:28:13.817
Everyone. we'll be able to take care
of this issue faster

500
00:28:13.900 --> 00:28:15.985
if you all head back first.

501
00:28:16.069 --> 00:28:18.363
-Do something about the elevators.
-Everyone.

502
00:28:18.446 --> 00:28:20.281
-Please.
-How will you take care of this?

503
00:28:20.365 --> 00:28:22.325
Are you even doing your jobs?

504
00:28:22.409 --> 00:28:24.285
We live on the 28th floor.

505
00:28:24.369 --> 00:28:27.163
Can you fix it before my kid comes home?

506
00:28:27.247 --> 00:28:30.250
Everyone. I'm a resident here as well.

507
00:28:30.333 --> 00:28:31.543
I had to walk too.

508
00:28:31.626 --> 00:28:34.754
If you give us time.
we'll handle this as soon as possible.

509
00:28:34.838 --> 00:28:36.881
Mr. Choi. let's call an emergency meeting.

510
00:28:36.965 --> 00:28:38.341
Yes. sir.

511
00:28:40.427 --> 00:28:41.928
That's not the problem right now.

512
00:28:42.011 --> 00:28:43.680
How will we go upstairs?

513
00:28:44.180 --> 00:28:47.350
RESIDENTS' ASSOCIATION
ELEVATOR BREAKDOWN RESPONSE MEETING

514
00:28:47.434 --> 00:28:48.768
How will you take care of this?

515
00:28:49.561 --> 00:28:52.313
Everyone. please calm down.

516
00:28:52.397 --> 00:28:54.357
Let's hear from our president first.

517
00:28:55.942 --> 00:28:57.110
To tell you the truth.

518
00:28:57.193 --> 00:29:00.447
because of a strike
at the factory overseas.

519
00:29:00.530 --> 00:29:02.615
they say it'll take a year
for the parts to arrive.

520
00:29:03.533 --> 00:29:05.952
-How can we wait a year?
-That makes no sense!

521
00:29:06.035 --> 00:29:07.328
How can we wait an entire year?

522
00:29:07.412 --> 00:29:09.205
Do something. President Park!

523
00:29:09.289 --> 00:29:11.499
We're checking with companies in Korea

524
00:29:11.583 --> 00:29:13.752
to see if anyone has the parts.

525
00:29:13.835 --> 00:29:15.086
so let's wait a bit longer.

526
00:29:16.087 --> 00:29:18.381
You're always just asking us to wait.

527
00:29:18.465 --> 00:29:20.258
-How long do we have to wait?
-Right?

528
00:29:20.341 --> 00:29:22.218
It might be fine
for those on the lower floors.

529
00:29:22.302 --> 00:29:24.804
but people living on higher floors
can't keep enduring this.

530
00:29:24.888 --> 00:29:26.973
This is ridiculous!

531
00:29:27.056 --> 00:29:29.559
My mother will collapse
climbing the stairs!

532
00:29:35.356 --> 00:29:36.816
That is why

533
00:29:36.900 --> 00:29:39.235
I am proposing
to replace all the elevators

534
00:29:39.319 --> 00:29:42.447
to prevent the continuous breakdowns

535
00:29:43.114 --> 00:29:45.450
and any future safety issues.

536
00:29:47.327 --> 00:29:48.536
I can't believe this.

537
00:29:48.620 --> 00:29:50.747
-That's easier said than done.
-Excuse me…

538
00:29:50.830 --> 00:29:51.998
-It takes time and money.
-So…

539
00:29:53.124 --> 00:29:56.127
That would cost a fortune.

540
00:29:56.211 --> 00:29:57.378
How would you pay for that?

541
00:29:57.462 --> 00:29:59.798
Is it possible
with the current reserve fund?

542
00:29:59.881 --> 00:30:00.840
You're right.

543
00:30:01.883 --> 00:30:03.927
Our reserve fund isn't enough.

544
00:30:04.803 --> 00:30:07.680
We currently have
about 17 billion in the fund.

545
00:30:07.764 --> 00:30:11.518
but we'd need approximately 20 billion
to replace the elevators

546
00:30:11.601 --> 00:30:13.436
in every building.

547
00:30:13.520 --> 00:30:14.771
Twenty billion?

548
00:30:14.854 --> 00:30:16.231
Oh my gosh.

549
00:30:16.314 --> 00:30:19.526
-Then we'd have to pay for the rest.
-President Park.

550
00:30:20.360 --> 00:30:23.988
You don't seem to be aware of this.

551
00:30:24.072 --> 00:30:28.827
but the elevators
have been breaking down for a long time.

552
00:30:28.910 --> 00:30:31.371
It's been like this
ever since we first moved here.

553
00:30:31.454 --> 00:30:32.914
-Exactly.
-Right.

554
00:30:32.997 --> 00:30:36.167
We should really just
file a lawsuit this time.

555
00:30:36.251 --> 00:30:37.836
Let's sue the company!

556
00:30:38.628 --> 00:30:39.963
We should!

557
00:30:41.965 --> 00:30:43.132
A lawsuit?

558
00:30:44.217 --> 00:30:46.761
The defect repair period is already over.

559
00:30:47.345 --> 00:30:50.014
I know it's upsetting.
but you should've done it sooner.

560
00:30:50.098 --> 00:30:51.224
You stayed quiet until now.

561
00:30:51.307 --> 00:30:54.310
but you blame the company
after the defect repair period is over?

562
00:30:54.394 --> 00:30:56.479
That would only look
like you're throwing a fit.

563
00:30:56.563 --> 00:30:58.815
What's more.
our opponent is a large company.

564
00:30:58.898 --> 00:31:03.152
They'll hire
the best law firm in Korea to fight us.

565
00:31:03.236 --> 00:31:05.280
And if we lose that fight.

566
00:31:05.363 --> 00:31:08.324
we'll all have to bear
the enormous cost of that lawsuit.

567
00:31:08.408 --> 00:31:09.951
Are you willing to take that risk?

568
00:31:14.706 --> 00:31:16.082
-I have a headache.
-Then…

569
00:31:16.833 --> 00:31:18.626
what are you suggesting?

570
00:31:20.044 --> 00:31:21.921
I am sincerely urging you

571
00:31:22.005 --> 00:31:25.341
to understand that an increase
in the reserve fund fee is inevitable.

572
00:31:26.634 --> 00:31:29.429
That damn reserve fund…

573
00:31:29.512 --> 00:31:30.972
We have to pay more?

574
00:31:35.810 --> 00:31:39.939
Everyone. will you buy convenience
for the cost of one chicken?

575
00:31:40.023 --> 00:31:42.317
Or will you keep living in fear.
riding an elevator

576
00:31:42.400 --> 00:31:44.277
that could break down at any moment?

577
00:31:45.486 --> 00:31:46.738
Your choice

578
00:31:47.989 --> 00:31:49.365
will change your future.

579
00:31:53.453 --> 00:31:55.496
I'm just going to vote yes.

580
00:31:55.997 --> 00:31:58.750
It's not like the reserve fund
is going to disappear.

581
00:31:58.833 --> 00:32:01.002
It's going back
into the apartment complex.

582
00:32:02.795 --> 00:32:04.547
No. I can't deliver it on foot.

583
00:32:04.631 --> 00:32:07.008
{\an8}I'm on the first floor. Please come down.

584
00:32:09.510 --> 00:32:10.678
It's Unit 2802.

585
00:32:11.888 --> 00:32:12.889
Thank you.

586
00:32:14.223 --> 00:32:16.935
I'm getting delivery
because I don't want to cook.

587
00:32:17.018 --> 00:32:19.228
but this is going to kill my knees.

588
00:32:20.104 --> 00:32:22.023
Whatever. I'm just going to vote yes.

589
00:32:22.106 --> 00:32:25.985
How can the elderly live like this?

590
00:32:26.069 --> 00:32:28.237
-My goodness…
-Just a moment.

591
00:32:28.321 --> 00:32:30.865
Mother. let's get some rest here.

592
00:32:30.949 --> 00:32:32.575
Gosh. my knees.

593
00:32:36.579 --> 00:32:39.123
Money isn't the problem right now.

594
00:32:41.751 --> 00:32:43.044
Be careful.

595
00:32:43.127 --> 00:32:45.421
Did you hear they're doubling
the reserve fund fee?

596
00:32:45.505 --> 00:32:46.839
Yeah.

597
00:32:47.465 --> 00:32:49.175
Double the fee would be tough.

598
00:32:50.343 --> 00:32:52.637
We're only renting.

599
00:32:52.720 --> 00:32:54.806
Even if we pay it
and they replace the elevators.

600
00:32:54.889 --> 00:32:57.558
we can get all the fees back
when we move out.

601
00:32:58.226 --> 00:32:59.978
We have nothing to lose.

602
00:33:01.312 --> 00:33:02.188
Are you happy?

603
00:33:02.271 --> 00:33:04.107
Are you happy that we're renting?

604
00:33:04.607 --> 00:33:05.984
Yeah. I am.

605
00:33:08.987 --> 00:33:11.072
Why did the elevators have to break down

606
00:33:11.155 --> 00:33:12.949
right after President Park got elected?

607
00:33:13.032 --> 00:33:14.617
Those damn elevators.

608
00:33:16.077 --> 00:33:18.204
He could become a lame duck at this rate.

609
00:33:18.871 --> 00:33:19.914
What time is it?

610
00:33:21.457 --> 00:33:23.418
Gosh. Is the vote closed now?

611
00:33:40.727 --> 00:33:41.853
What time is it?

612
00:33:42.854 --> 00:33:44.689
It's 6:30.

613
00:33:45.189 --> 00:33:46.274
The vote closed at 6:00.

614
00:33:46.357 --> 00:33:48.359
The results should've
been out immediately.

615
00:33:48.860 --> 00:33:50.403
Why aren't they announcing it?

616
00:33:55.199 --> 00:33:57.827
I'll go to the office myself and check…

617
00:33:59.412 --> 00:34:01.414
<i>This is the management office.</i>

618
00:34:01.497 --> 00:34:03.124
<i>We'll announce the results</i>

619
00:34:03.207 --> 00:34:07.420
<i>of the vote on increasing</i>
<i>the long-term repair reserve fund fee.</i>

620
00:34:07.503 --> 00:34:11.132
<i>Of the 7.237 households</i>
<i>that participated in the vote.</i>

621
00:34:11.215 --> 00:34:13.593
<i>52.7% were in favor.</i>

622
00:34:13.676 --> 00:34:16.637
<i>-and 47.3% were against.</i>
-We did it.

623
00:34:16.721 --> 00:34:19.432
<i>The proposal to increase the fee</i>
<i>has been approved.</i>

624
00:34:32.153 --> 00:34:33.446
Double the reserve fund!

625
00:34:34.155 --> 00:34:35.948
Wow!

626
00:34:36.032 --> 00:34:38.367
Double the reserve fund fee!

627
00:34:41.287 --> 00:34:43.790
<i>The increased</i>
<i>long-term repair reserve fund fee</i>

628
00:34:43.873 --> 00:34:47.502
<i>will be reflected in the maintenance fees</i>
<i>starting this month.</i>

629
00:34:47.585 --> 00:34:50.630
<i>We kindly ask</i>
<i>for your support and cooperation.</i>

630
00:34:50.713 --> 00:34:52.965
<i>-Thank you.</i>
-Park Hae-kang is amazing.

631
00:34:53.674 --> 00:34:57.345
He really is quite the talent.

632
00:34:57.428 --> 00:35:00.098
He really increased the reserve fund fee.

633
00:35:00.681 --> 00:35:01.891
It seems…

634
00:35:02.683 --> 00:35:04.435
I've gotten

635
00:35:04.519 --> 00:35:07.980
a much better replacement.

636
00:35:10.274 --> 00:35:12.193
Sorry for asking to meet
at such a late hour.

637
00:35:12.944 --> 00:35:15.404
All the management companies
are yours. aren't they?

638
00:35:15.488 --> 00:35:18.741
Oh. I was trying
not to make it so obvious.

639
00:35:18.825 --> 00:35:19.784
Could you tell?

640
00:35:19.867 --> 00:35:21.994
Call the elevator repair company.

641
00:35:22.620 --> 00:35:23.621
Why?

642
00:35:23.704 --> 00:35:25.206
I need to stop the elevators.

643
00:35:25.289 --> 00:35:26.290
Why?

644
00:35:26.374 --> 00:35:27.875
I'm different from President Seo.

645
00:35:27.959 --> 00:35:29.961
Just keeping the money is no fun.

646
00:35:30.545 --> 00:35:31.838
I told you.

647
00:35:31.921 --> 00:35:34.006
just keeping it is hard enough.

648
00:35:34.090 --> 00:35:35.466
I'd like to increase it.

649
00:35:35.550 --> 00:35:37.135
not just protect it.

650
00:35:39.137 --> 00:35:40.346
My money?

651
00:35:50.022 --> 00:35:52.608
I did as you asked. Mr. Park.

652
00:35:53.359 --> 00:35:54.819
But isn't this a huge gamble?

653
00:35:55.403 --> 00:35:57.196
If it is. what would you bet on?

654
00:35:59.198 --> 00:36:00.116
I don't bet anything

655
00:36:00.199 --> 00:36:03.911
on something I'm not certain of.

656
00:36:04.579 --> 00:36:05.580
Gambling

657
00:36:05.663 --> 00:36:08.416
is what desperate people do.

658
00:36:11.169 --> 00:36:13.379
You must be quite anxious.

659
00:36:16.132 --> 00:36:17.884
You're more of a coward than I thought.

660
00:36:19.594 --> 00:36:23.097
I don't start any games
that I'm not confident in.

661
00:36:25.516 --> 00:36:26.684
You're very cool.

662
00:36:38.571 --> 00:36:41.616
Why does Park Hae-kang
keep making my heart flutter?

663
00:36:42.325 --> 00:36:43.826
This is bad.

664
00:36:44.493 --> 00:36:45.578
Oh. right.

665
00:36:45.661 --> 00:36:47.413
I have to do what he asked.

666
00:36:47.997 --> 00:36:49.582
I already called the company.

667
00:36:49.665 --> 00:36:52.335
They'll get the elevators
working again tonight.

668
00:36:53.336 --> 00:36:54.253
But…

669
00:36:54.837 --> 00:36:58.174
the residents won't just sit still
if you don't replace them.

670
00:37:01.052 --> 00:37:03.721
Park Hae-kang said we'd need 20 billion.

671
00:37:03.804 --> 00:37:06.432
so they'll wait
until it reaches that amount.

672
00:37:06.515 --> 00:37:08.142
And after that.

673
00:37:08.226 --> 00:37:10.770
we can just give another reason
to postpone it.

674
00:37:11.354 --> 00:37:12.897
People forget things easily.

675
00:37:14.023 --> 00:37:14.857
Yes. sir.

676
00:37:16.025 --> 00:37:18.277
-There's something to report.
-Go on.

677
00:37:18.361 --> 00:37:22.490
The man Park Hae-kang was meeting
was an official in the police.

678
00:37:23.241 --> 00:37:25.576
Chief of Investigation. Son Dae-un.

679
00:37:26.077 --> 00:37:28.996
He was the one who busted
Park's gambling den in Gangnam.

680
00:37:30.414 --> 00:37:32.667
Then why would they meet up secretly?

681
00:37:32.750 --> 00:37:34.502
It seems Chief Son

682
00:37:34.585 --> 00:37:37.630
is holding Park Yong-man.
the former Oasis Gang boss. hostage.

683
00:37:37.713 --> 00:37:40.299
He took Park Hae-kang in.

684
00:37:40.383 --> 00:37:43.135
Park Yong-man is currently being held
at a detention center.

685
00:37:47.014 --> 00:37:49.976
So that's why Park Hae-kang needed money.

686
00:37:50.059 --> 00:37:51.602
To get his old boss out.

687
00:37:52.103 --> 00:37:53.229
But sir.

688
00:37:53.813 --> 00:37:57.400
Chief Son is connected
to the commissioner.

689
00:37:58.818 --> 00:37:59.777
The commissioner?

690
00:37:59.860 --> 00:38:03.447
The commissioner who's desperate
to join our One Club?

691
00:38:04.240 --> 00:38:05.449
Yes. that's right.

692
00:38:09.036 --> 00:38:11.414
Things are getting very interesting.

693
00:38:12.623 --> 00:38:13.499
Mr. Kim.

694
00:38:14.834 --> 00:38:19.171
We're going to get
double the reserve fund fees now.

695
00:38:20.339 --> 00:38:23.092
Then there's another matter
to take care of.

696
00:38:23.759 --> 00:38:26.804
Let's leave after just five more minutes.

697
00:38:37.982 --> 00:38:40.818
What on earth is President Park thinking?

698
00:38:42.111 --> 00:38:43.321
Could he…

699
00:38:45.865 --> 00:38:48.909
be aware that we don't have the fund?

700
00:38:50.328 --> 00:38:52.413
No. He could never tell from the papers.

701
00:39:02.798 --> 00:39:03.924
Oh dear.

702
00:39:05.134 --> 00:39:07.219
You're working late.

703
00:39:11.599 --> 00:39:13.559
Ha-jeong. can I talk to you for a moment?

704
00:39:14.894 --> 00:39:16.479
Mr. Choi. sit down.

705
00:39:16.562 --> 00:39:18.230
We're a family.

706
00:39:18.314 --> 00:39:19.607
Come on. Sit.

707
00:39:26.530 --> 00:39:28.991
What is this about?

708
00:39:29.075 --> 00:39:31.202
We're working on the elevator issue…

709
00:39:31.285 --> 00:39:32.912
It's not about that.

710
00:39:34.288 --> 00:39:35.790
Sir…

711
00:39:36.874 --> 00:39:37.958
What is it?

712
00:39:39.126 --> 00:39:41.170
I'd like to come clean

713
00:39:42.338 --> 00:39:43.714
about something to you too.

714
00:39:45.299 --> 00:39:48.052
I really like the ledger
that you organized.

715
00:39:48.135 --> 00:39:49.762
Ms. Kang.

716
00:39:50.429 --> 00:39:53.265
Even to me. it seems flawless.

717
00:39:58.479 --> 00:39:59.563
It's me.

718
00:40:00.523 --> 00:40:02.108
The guy who's taking the reserve fund.

719
00:40:11.117 --> 00:40:13.911
You're making me embarrassed
with that reaction.

720
00:40:14.495 --> 00:40:15.955
I'm not here to startle you.

721
00:40:16.038 --> 00:40:18.207
I'm sorry if I shocked you.

722
00:40:19.458 --> 00:40:20.835
The thing is.

723
00:40:21.836 --> 00:40:24.713
I love the way you work. Ms. Kang.

724
00:40:25.840 --> 00:40:28.008
But I heard you wanted to quit.

725
00:40:31.095 --> 00:40:34.640
Was there anything that displeased you?

726
00:40:38.436 --> 00:40:39.770
Was the pay too small?

727
00:40:40.646 --> 00:40:42.481
No. it's nothing like that.

728
00:40:42.565 --> 00:40:43.649
Or…

729
00:40:43.732 --> 00:40:46.986
how about joining
Taesan Construction's finance team?

730
00:40:47.736 --> 00:40:49.613
It's a better workplace than this.

731
00:40:49.697 --> 00:40:52.324
and you can proudly tell your family
it's a large company.

732
00:40:53.242 --> 00:40:54.118
What do you say?

733
00:40:56.787 --> 00:40:57.830
Ms. Kang.

734
00:40:58.539 --> 00:41:01.834
I'm offering you a job right now.

735
00:41:01.917 --> 00:41:05.504
I'll give you twice your current salary.

736
00:41:05.588 --> 00:41:06.630
Why aren't you answering?

737
00:41:07.339 --> 00:41:08.924
He's asking you a question.

738
00:41:18.809 --> 00:41:20.686
I'M SORRY. HA-JEONG

739
00:41:20.769 --> 00:41:24.523
So you're supposed to draw your family?

740
00:41:25.024 --> 00:41:25.900
Yes.

741
00:41:27.234 --> 00:41:28.527
Let's see…

742
00:41:31.864 --> 00:41:33.532
Why have you been sighing all day?

743
00:41:33.616 --> 00:41:35.868
You're a young lady
with a whole future ahead of you.

744
00:41:37.286 --> 00:41:40.789
That future has already
turned into a tangled mess.

745
00:41:42.166 --> 00:41:44.168
You said you're a professional.

746
00:41:44.835 --> 00:41:47.630
You should stick to your role
and help your kid with his homework.

747
00:41:47.713 --> 00:41:50.174
Sometimes. moms can be depressed too.

748
00:41:50.257 --> 00:41:52.134
You and that smart mouth of yours…

749
00:41:54.887 --> 00:41:56.555
Ta-da. It's Dad. Park Hae-kang.

750
00:41:56.639 --> 00:41:58.057
It looks just like him. right?

751
00:41:58.140 --> 00:42:00.768
Isn't Park Hae-kang
a bit more handsome than that?

752
00:42:03.771 --> 00:42:06.690
Do you really have to correct him
even when you're depressed?

753
00:42:07.733 --> 00:42:10.694
Facts are important
to seven-year-olds. you know.

754
00:42:11.403 --> 00:42:12.404
Geez.

755
00:42:15.407 --> 00:42:16.325
You know

756
00:42:16.992 --> 00:42:19.036
I can't stand people being bad at stuff.

757
00:42:19.119 --> 00:42:21.705
Let's do your homework based on facts.

758
00:42:21.789 --> 00:42:22.998
Okay.

759
00:42:25.084 --> 00:42:26.710
What color should we use?

760
00:42:30.381 --> 00:42:32.925
But aren't you going home? It's past 6:00.

761
00:42:34.843 --> 00:42:36.303
I'm working overtime today.

762
00:42:36.387 --> 00:42:37.221
Overtime?

763
00:42:37.846 --> 00:42:39.390
Mr. Park makes you work overtime?

764
00:42:39.473 --> 00:42:42.560
That brat.
Just report him to the Ministry of Labor.

765
00:42:42.643 --> 00:42:45.062
No. this is voluntary overtime.

766
00:42:45.854 --> 00:42:47.731
You don't even like your job.

767
00:42:47.815 --> 00:42:50.025
What do you mean. "voluntary overtime"?

768
00:42:52.444 --> 00:42:55.197
If you're going to keep sighing.
just go home.

769
00:42:55.281 --> 00:42:58.158
Or at least tell me what's going on.

770
00:42:59.118 --> 00:43:00.786
I just have something on my mind.

771
00:43:02.454 --> 00:43:04.456
Uncle Big Guy…

772
00:43:23.100 --> 00:43:25.769
I'm thinking of transferring
to a place with a higher salary.

773
00:43:26.520 --> 00:43:27.396
You…

774
00:43:29.773 --> 00:43:31.108
should start studying again.

775
00:43:32.776 --> 00:43:34.653
Quit everything else

776
00:43:34.737 --> 00:43:36.447
and focus on your studies.

777
00:43:36.530 --> 00:43:38.157
I'll do whatever it takes to support you.

778
00:43:38.240 --> 00:43:39.617
Ha-jeong.

779
00:43:39.700 --> 00:43:41.994
just go live your own life.

780
00:43:42.077 --> 00:43:43.912
Stop worrying about mine.

781
00:43:43.996 --> 00:43:46.040
How can you say that to me?

782
00:43:46.123 --> 00:43:47.124
I can.

783
00:43:47.791 --> 00:43:49.418
I have to.

784
00:43:49.501 --> 00:43:52.630
Just please stop wasting your own life
to support mine.

785
00:43:53.172 --> 00:43:54.256
That's enough.

786
00:43:55.007 --> 00:43:56.216
Get back to your studies.

787
00:43:56.300 --> 00:43:58.302
You should take the bar exam again.

788
00:43:58.385 --> 00:44:00.137
I'll handle this on my own.

789
00:44:00.220 --> 00:44:01.055
Ha-ri!

790
00:44:03.766 --> 00:44:05.976
I'm really sorry I lied to you.

791
00:44:07.436 --> 00:44:08.896
but I'm not quitting this gig.

792
00:44:09.438 --> 00:44:10.439
What?

793
00:44:11.315 --> 00:44:12.274
Ha-jeong.

794
00:44:16.028 --> 00:44:17.655
I've already failed.

795
00:44:24.161 --> 00:44:26.372
So you should accept that too.

796
00:44:29.041 --> 00:44:30.250
Someone told me

797
00:44:31.585 --> 00:44:34.380
that there are things you see
only after you fail.

798
00:44:36.465 --> 00:44:37.549
And what I saw…

799
00:44:38.926 --> 00:44:41.136
is you.

800
00:44:41.220 --> 00:44:43.806
I saw your life
that's been tied down by me.

801
00:44:49.728 --> 00:44:51.647
-Ha-ri. I--
-I'm grateful.

802
00:44:52.564 --> 00:44:54.733
I'm really grateful for the youth

803
00:44:55.484 --> 00:44:57.069
that you wasted because of me.

804
00:44:59.363 --> 00:45:01.615
And I'm really sorry.

805
00:45:07.496 --> 00:45:09.289
I'm going to start over.

806
00:45:11.458 --> 00:45:13.377
I'll achieve my dream on my own now.

807
00:45:37.067 --> 00:45:38.694
Why am I even here?

808
00:45:41.655 --> 00:45:43.240
Why do you keep crying?

809
00:45:48.704 --> 00:45:51.748
The debt collectors
were pressuring me today.

810
00:45:56.128 --> 00:45:58.922
Don't worry about me and go home.

811
00:46:23.906 --> 00:46:25.699
Please let me stay the night.

812
00:46:35.042 --> 00:46:36.835
Boss. why are you…

813
00:46:39.046 --> 00:46:40.964
Ms. Kang. why are you…

814
00:46:41.048 --> 00:46:42.925
What?

815
00:46:46.470 --> 00:46:47.804
Everyone. get up!

816
00:46:48.305 --> 00:46:49.848
Come out here!

817
00:46:49.932 --> 00:46:51.141
-What?
-What is it?

818
00:46:51.225 --> 00:46:52.392
Everyone. come out here!

819
00:46:52.476 --> 00:46:53.519
What?

820
00:46:53.602 --> 00:46:56.230
-What is it?
-Did you two…

821
00:46:57.064 --> 00:46:58.106
-What?
-Did you two…

822
00:46:58.190 --> 00:46:59.608
What is it?

823
00:47:00.692 --> 00:47:02.277
I'll pretend I didn't see that.

824
00:47:02.361 --> 00:47:04.321
-No. it's not like that.
-You got the wrong idea.

825
00:47:04.404 --> 00:47:05.781
What's going on?

826
00:47:05.864 --> 00:47:07.407
What is it?

827
00:47:07.491 --> 00:47:10.410
Ms. Kang just came out of the bedroom.

828
00:47:12.412 --> 00:47:14.373
What's wrong with that?
They're both young.

829
00:47:14.456 --> 00:47:16.875
People had children even during wars.

830
00:47:16.959 --> 00:47:18.710
-What are you saying?
-Children?

831
00:47:18.794 --> 00:47:21.797
Boss. you can tell us the truth.

832
00:47:21.880 --> 00:47:23.048
You really…

833
00:47:23.131 --> 00:47:24.883
No. we were the ones who were clueless.

834
00:47:24.967 --> 00:47:27.094
We'll spend the night
somewhere else twice a week!

835
00:47:27.177 --> 00:47:29.346
-All of you. stop it!
-You brat…

836
00:47:29.429 --> 00:47:32.015
From an intermittent family
to a real family…

837
00:47:33.016 --> 00:47:34.226
A love story?

838
00:47:34.309 --> 00:47:35.894
-No. a soap opera!
-A soap opera!

839
00:47:36.853 --> 00:47:38.605
Let's give them some privacy today!

840
00:47:38.689 --> 00:47:40.524
-All right.
-Come on. Let's go.

841
00:47:42.943 --> 00:47:43.777
I had no idea.

842
00:47:46.530 --> 00:47:47.573
What?

843
00:47:48.240 --> 00:47:49.825
-Why…
-Bye. then.

844
00:47:49.908 --> 00:47:51.451
What's with you guys?

845
00:47:51.535 --> 00:47:52.786
We'll be back later.

846
00:47:55.289 --> 00:47:57.124
Hit the elevator button.

847
00:47:58.458 --> 00:47:59.459
Come here.

848
00:48:03.672 --> 00:48:04.506
Gosh.

849
00:48:23.233 --> 00:48:26.069
Gentlemen. have some snacks.

850
00:48:26.153 --> 00:48:27.738
Gather round.

851
00:48:27.821 --> 00:48:29.656
That must be tasty.

852
00:48:30.949 --> 00:48:32.200
Great timing. I was hungry.

853
00:48:32.284 --> 00:48:33.744
Come on.

854
00:48:37.664 --> 00:48:38.665
All right.

855
00:48:44.129 --> 00:48:46.923
I bought these from a restaurant
going viral on social media.

856
00:48:47.507 --> 00:48:48.634
I waited two hours.

857
00:48:52.179 --> 00:48:53.388
It was worth the wait.

858
00:48:54.348 --> 00:48:55.849
Let me pack any leftovers

859
00:48:55.932 --> 00:48:57.434
so I can give them to my wife.

860
00:48:59.811 --> 00:49:01.772
You have to be good to your wife
when you're old.

861
00:49:01.855 --> 00:49:03.357
She's your retirement plan.

862
00:49:04.358 --> 00:49:06.109
You must be in a good mood today.

863
00:49:07.361 --> 00:49:08.487
I am.

864
00:49:08.570 --> 00:49:10.781
But it's not because of you.

865
00:49:11.531 --> 00:49:12.991
You can listen while you eat.

866
00:49:13.533 --> 00:49:15.410
After a long wait.

867
00:49:16.411 --> 00:49:18.497
our Oman New Town project
is back on track.

868
00:49:18.580 --> 00:49:19.831
Let's drink to that.

869
00:49:21.041 --> 00:49:22.834
-Congratulations.
-Cheers!

870
00:49:28.382 --> 00:49:29.800
As promised.

871
00:49:29.883 --> 00:49:33.345
money will start pouring
into your pockets now.

872
00:49:33.428 --> 00:49:35.347
So who should you be good to?

873
00:49:35.430 --> 00:49:36.932
Your retirement

874
00:49:37.015 --> 00:49:39.893
isn't secured by a wife
who can cheat on you anytime.

875
00:49:40.894 --> 00:49:42.771
It's secured by money.

876
00:49:44.064 --> 00:49:46.566
I'll be the one
taking care of your future now.

877
00:49:47.150 --> 00:49:48.652
so you should be good to me.

878
00:49:48.735 --> 00:49:49.653
Don't you think?

879
00:49:50.153 --> 00:49:53.198
Right. You're better than my own son.

880
00:49:55.117 --> 00:49:56.576
You did a great job.

881
00:49:56.660 --> 00:49:59.079
Isn't it nice to have
construction resume again?

882
00:49:59.162 --> 00:50:02.124
Yes. Very nice.

883
00:50:05.210 --> 00:50:07.087
Getting everything handed to you.

884
00:50:12.092 --> 00:50:14.177
You're very lucky to have all that

885
00:50:14.761 --> 00:50:16.012
without lifting a finger.

886
00:50:17.055 --> 00:50:19.099
-Come on.
-Eat up. everyone.

887
00:50:21.685 --> 00:50:22.644
Sir.

888
00:50:23.478 --> 00:50:25.647
Commissioner Kwak Ju-gwon is here.

889
00:50:34.906 --> 00:50:36.324
What is this?

890
00:50:37.325 --> 00:50:41.329
I got these valuable ginseng roots
especially for you.

891
00:50:42.164 --> 00:50:44.332
hoping they'll help restore your energy.

892
00:50:50.630 --> 00:50:52.549
Ginseng doesn't agree with me.

893
00:50:52.632 --> 00:50:54.050
I have too much heat in my body.

894
00:50:54.801 --> 00:50:55.802
You can have them.

895
00:50:56.595 --> 00:50:57.637
Pardon?

896
00:50:58.972 --> 00:51:00.098
By the way.

897
00:51:00.766 --> 00:51:03.727
how's the ten billion won coming along?

898
00:51:04.936 --> 00:51:06.480
Yes. well…

899
00:51:06.980 --> 00:51:08.899
My men are getting it prepared.

900
00:51:08.982 --> 00:51:11.359
Your men? Not yourself?

901
00:51:11.443 --> 00:51:13.069
Well.

902
00:51:13.153 --> 00:51:14.863
there are friends helping me.

903
00:51:15.989 --> 00:51:17.407
So you're extorting it.

904
00:51:18.158 --> 00:51:20.911
Oh. goodness.

905
00:51:22.037 --> 00:51:23.747
Extorting?

906
00:51:23.830 --> 00:51:25.040
I'm just getting help.

907
00:51:25.832 --> 00:51:29.461
I built a lot of connections
during my years as a cop.

908
00:51:29.544 --> 00:51:31.963
And which of those connections

909
00:51:32.047 --> 00:51:34.382
is getting you ten billion won?

910
00:51:37.511 --> 00:51:39.262
It's a guy who used to run a gambling den.

911
00:51:39.346 --> 00:51:42.182
He's a pro when it comes to getting money.

912
00:51:44.351 --> 00:51:45.811
A guy who ran a gambling den?

913
00:51:45.894 --> 00:51:46.978
Yes.

914
00:51:52.275 --> 00:51:54.152
His name's Park Hae-kang.

915
00:51:54.861 --> 00:51:56.613
-Park Hoe-kwang?
-No.

916
00:51:57.239 --> 00:51:59.157
Hae-kang.

917
00:52:00.075 --> 00:52:01.910
-Park Hae-kang?
-Yes.

918
00:52:02.828 --> 00:52:05.831
How do you know such a competent guy?

919
00:52:07.666 --> 00:52:10.627
Can you introduce me to him later?

920
00:52:12.128 --> 00:52:14.089
Sure. I will.

921
00:52:15.006 --> 00:52:17.050
I'll leave this with you.

922
00:52:40.782 --> 00:52:41.825
President Park.

923
00:52:41.908 --> 00:52:44.828
The 100% increase in the reserve fund fee.

924
00:52:45.412 --> 00:52:47.831
I was really touched by what you achieved.

925
00:52:47.914 --> 00:52:50.959
Can I give you a hug?

926
00:52:58.258 --> 00:53:01.595
You're making my heart pound these days.

927
00:53:02.554 --> 00:53:03.805
I'm so excited.

928
00:53:10.020 --> 00:53:11.730
Is it your first time in a penthouse?

929
00:53:11.813 --> 00:53:13.189
It's nothing special.

930
00:53:13.273 --> 00:53:14.357
The ceiling's high.

931
00:53:14.441 --> 00:53:17.360
but besides that.
it's no different from other houses.

932
00:53:18.278 --> 00:53:20.280
So have I proven that I'm better

933
00:53:21.281 --> 00:53:22.365
than President Seo?

934
00:53:24.618 --> 00:53:26.119
Of course.

935
00:53:26.703 --> 00:53:28.204
Thinking back now.

936
00:53:28.288 --> 00:53:31.124
President Seo was really useless.

937
00:53:32.125 --> 00:53:33.126
Very incompetent.

938
00:53:33.960 --> 00:53:37.047
I despise incompetent people the most.

939
00:53:37.797 --> 00:53:40.050
Then will you let me be the keeper

940
00:53:40.634 --> 00:53:41.843
of your vault?

941
00:53:43.011 --> 00:53:46.556
You are the perfect man
to take on that position.

942
00:53:51.186 --> 00:53:52.479
I'll count on you.

943
00:53:52.979 --> 00:53:56.107
I believe we'll make a great team.

944
00:53:56.191 --> 00:53:57.192
Don't you agree?

945
00:54:07.744 --> 00:54:10.288
I do feel bad putting you to work

946
00:54:10.372 --> 00:54:13.959
as soon as you've joined me
without even a honeymoon period.

947
00:54:14.709 --> 00:54:17.253
but I have an urgent favor to ask you.

948
00:54:18.046 --> 00:54:18.922
Sure.

949
00:54:19.422 --> 00:54:20.674
It's nothing difficult.

950
00:54:21.341 --> 00:54:23.593
Just take some money from Mr. Kim

951
00:54:23.677 --> 00:54:26.680
and deliver it to an apartment complex
in Gunam City.

952
00:54:27.514 --> 00:54:31.351
It's actually another complex
that I'm skimming from.

953
00:54:32.477 --> 00:54:35.438
I'm just putting back the money
I took out of there.

954
00:54:36.439 --> 00:54:39.818
There's going to be an audit soon.
so I'll get it back afterward.

955
00:54:41.361 --> 00:54:42.445
I understand.

956
00:54:43.613 --> 00:54:47.367
This is actually
what President Seo used to do.

957
00:54:47.450 --> 00:54:50.036
So think of this as training for the job.

958
00:54:51.079 --> 00:54:52.330
I'm counting on you.

959
00:55:16.646 --> 00:55:18.648
-Hey. Gyeong-nam.
<i>-Boss.</i>

960
00:55:18.732 --> 00:55:20.692
We tracked President Seo's whereabouts.

961
00:55:20.775 --> 00:55:23.111
and the last signal from his phone
came from Taegowon.

962
00:55:24.529 --> 00:55:26.114
-Taegowon?
<i>-Yes.</i>

963
00:55:26.698 --> 00:55:29.034
Je-gil hacked the security cams there.

964
00:55:29.659 --> 00:55:32.328
but he didn't ever see him
leave the premises.

965
00:55:33.246 --> 00:55:35.248
<i>It seems like President Seo was taken out.</i>

966
00:55:36.124 --> 00:55:37.125
<i>And…</i>

967
00:55:37.208 --> 00:55:39.794
his entire family disappeared as well.

968
00:55:40.628 --> 00:55:41.880
-Disappeared?
<i>-Yes.</i>

969
00:55:41.963 --> 00:55:45.383
Their belongings are still there.
but his family's gone.

970
00:55:45.467 --> 00:55:47.969
<i>It's like someone just erased them.</i>

971
00:55:48.803 --> 00:55:49.679
<i>Boss.</i>

972
00:55:50.597 --> 00:55:52.182
becoming Lee Chung-won's vault keeper

973
00:55:53.391 --> 00:55:54.642
is dangerous.

974
00:55:56.895 --> 00:55:59.773
Just stop digging
into President Seo for now.

975
00:55:59.856 --> 00:56:01.191
All right.

976
00:56:06.488 --> 00:56:07.906
Taegowon…

977
00:56:48.530 --> 00:56:49.989
KIM HONG-HYEON

978
00:56:51.491 --> 00:56:52.659
LEE JAE-GU

979
00:57:07.757 --> 00:57:10.176
SEO GANG-WON

980
00:57:24.065 --> 00:57:26.651
There are names for each of the trees.
What are they?

981
00:57:28.987 --> 00:57:31.489
They're people who sacrificed themselves
for Taegowon.

982
00:57:32.157 --> 00:57:35.326
So they're like commemorative trees.

983
00:57:39.998 --> 00:57:40.832
This is ten billion.

984
00:58:12.030 --> 00:58:13.281
<i>I can't get him released.</i>

985
00:58:13.364 --> 00:58:15.366
But I'll let him get treatment outside.

986
00:58:15.867 --> 00:58:16.701
Anything else

987
00:58:16.784 --> 00:58:18.828
will be discussed
after you bring the money.

988
00:58:25.668 --> 00:58:27.253
MR. SON. SEOUL POLICE CHIEF

989
00:58:29.339 --> 00:58:30.298
Yes?

990
00:58:30.381 --> 00:58:32.383
<i>Hey. Mr. Park.</i>

991
00:58:32.467 --> 00:58:35.720
Did you know
Park Yong-man was terminally ill?

992
00:58:46.523 --> 00:58:48.399
Hey. you can't just stop like that!

993
00:58:54.739 --> 00:58:55.990
What did you just say?

994
00:58:58.785 --> 00:58:59.827
<i>You didn't know?</i>

995
00:58:59.911 --> 00:59:01.538
They say it's pancreatic cancer.

996
00:59:01.621 --> 00:59:03.206
He has about three months left.

997
00:59:04.040 --> 00:59:05.208
<i>So…</i>

998
00:59:05.291 --> 00:59:07.710
you'd better hurry
if you don't want him to die in there.

999
00:59:07.794 --> 00:59:08.836
<i>Get the ten billion.</i>

1000
00:59:12.090 --> 00:59:15.093
So the commissioner attacked Park Hae-kang

1001
00:59:15.176 --> 00:59:17.178
to give me ten billion won.

1002
00:59:17.262 --> 00:59:20.515
and that's why Park Hae-kang
was trying to take ten billion

1003
00:59:21.099 --> 00:59:23.560
from the reserve fund
in my apartment complex?

1004
00:59:24.435 --> 00:59:25.979
Mr. Kim.

1005
00:59:26.646 --> 00:59:30.900
I think I could get
the competent Park Hae-kang for free.

1006
00:59:31.943 --> 00:59:34.487
Do you trust Park Hae-kang?

1007
00:59:36.030 --> 00:59:38.032
I'm going to do one last test…

1008
00:59:40.577 --> 00:59:43.162
to see if I can trust him or not.

1009
00:59:57.385 --> 01:00:00.471
I'm bringing over the ten billion.
so release him.

1010
01:00:00.555 --> 01:00:01.723
Right now!

1011
01:00:10.732 --> 01:00:13.443
THE APARTMENT JOB

1012
01:00:37.550 --> 01:00:40.678
{\an8}<i>Hey. did you know that there are people</i>
<i>using our community sauna for free?</i>

1013
01:00:40.762 --> 01:00:42.347
{\an8}<i>-We use our cards to enter.</i>
-Unbelievable.

1014
01:00:42.430 --> 01:00:43.431
{\an8}<i>You should see this.</i>

1015
01:00:43.514 --> 01:00:45.391
{\an8}A complaint about people
using our facilities.

1016
01:00:45.475 --> 01:00:48.394
{\an8}<i>-They want a facial recognition system.</i>
-I can't do this any longer.

1017
01:00:48.478 --> 01:00:49.771
{\an8}<i>Use the reserve fund?</i>

1018
01:00:49.854 --> 01:00:51.064
{\an8}-No.
-No.

1019
01:00:51.147 --> 01:00:53.524
{\an8}<i>We need to find the people</i>
<i>and give them a warning.</i>

1020
01:00:53.608 --> 01:00:54.859
{\an8}It's a rental unit.

1021
01:00:54.942 --> 01:00:57.570
{\an8}<i>"Reveal the rental units." Nonsense.</i>

1022
01:00:57.654 --> 01:00:59.864
{\an8}<i>The rental units are the problem.</i>

1023
01:01:00.573 --> 01:01:03.034
{\an8}-Conflict.
<i>-Ms. Kang. can you work overtime today?</i>

1024
01:01:03.117 --> 01:01:04.494
{\an8}<i>Why Park Hae-kang?</i>

1025
01:01:04.577 --> 01:01:08.206
{\an8}<i>Park Hae-kang can see the bigger picture.</i>

1026
01:01:08.289 --> 01:01:09.332
{\an8}Can you do something for me?

1027
01:01:09.415 --> 01:01:11.417
{\an8}And when it's over.
I'll give you the ten billion.

1028
01:01:11.501 --> 01:01:13.419
{\an8}<i>You'd better hurry.</i>

1029
01:01:13.503 --> 01:01:16.881
{\an8}<i>because that ten billion you want</i>
<i>is on borrowed time too.</i>

1030
01:01:19.759 --> 01:01:21.761
Subtitle translation by: Juyoung Park

1031
01:01:22.305 --> 01:02:22.261
